---
layout: base.njk
pageTitle: Python for Renewable Energy & Grid GIS Automation
description: A production-focused resource for spatial workflows, compliance automation, and scalable geospatial pipelines in the renewable energy sector.
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: false
---
{% from "icons.njk" import icon %}

<section class="home-hero">
  <div class="container home-hero__inner">
    <img class="home-hero__logo" src="/assets/logo.svg" alt="{{ site.title }}" width="480" height="160">
    <h1>Python for Renewable Energy &amp; Grid GIS Automation</h1>
    <p class="home-hero__tag">{{ site.description }}</p>
    <p class="home-hero__intro">
      Solar irradiance mapping, wind resource assessment, grid proximity analysis, exclusion screening, least-cost interconnection routing, turbine layout, and audit-ready compliance reporting — all built with reproducible, memory-aware Python. This site is a working library for energy analysts, GIS developers, project developers, and environmental technology teams who deploy spatial workflows to production rather than the desktop.
    </p>
    <p class="home-hero__intro">
      Each section walks through a deterministic pipeline stage: coordinate-reference governance, raster &amp; vector ingestion, validation gates, constraint and exclusion screening, network topology and routing, resource-to-energy conversion, and the containerised orchestration that runs the whole thing unattended. Code is annotated, tested in real workflows, and tuned for cloud-scale execution against multi-gigabyte energy datasets.
    </p>
    <div class="home-ctas">
      {% for item in site.nav %}
        <a class="home-cta" href="{{ site.url }}{{ item.url }}" style="--cta-bg: {{ item.color }}1A;">
          <span class="home-cta__icon" style="background: {{ item.color }}22;">
            {{ icon(item.icon, item.color) }}
          </span>
          <span class="home-cta__text">
            <span class="home-cta__title">{{ item.label }}</span>
            <span class="home-cta__desc">{{ item.blurb }}</span>
          </span>
        </a>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="home-section">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>What you’ll find inside</h2>
    <p class="home-section__lede">
      Three deeply linked content tracks — each starting with an architectural overview and branching into focused, reproducible patterns: PV yield simulation, interconnection queue screening, wetland and floodplain exclusion, least-cost corridor routing, wake-loss estimation, terrain shading, cloud data ingestion, and quick-reference tables for projections, spatial indexes, and resampling kernels.
    </p>
    <ul class="home-cards" style="list-style:none; padding:0;">
      {% for item in site.nav %}
        {% set kids = collections.all | children(item.url) %}
        <li class="home-card" style="--card-c: {{ item.color }};">
          <a class="home-card__head" href="{{ site.url }}{{ item.url }}" style="text-decoration:none; color:inherit;">
            {{ icon(item.icon, item.color) }}
            <h3>{{ item.label }}</h3>
          </a>
          <p>{{ item.blurb }}</p>
          {% if kids.length %}
            <ul style="list-style:none; padding:0; margin:.5rem 0 0; display:grid; gap:.25rem;">
              {% for kid in kids %}
                <li><a href="{{ site.url }}{{ kid.url }}" style="font-size:.92rem;">{{ collections.all | titleFor(kid.url) }}</a></li>
              {% endfor %}
            </ul>
          {% endif %}
          <a class="home-card__more" href="{{ site.url }}{{ item.url }}">Open section {{ icon('arrow', 'currentColor') }}</a>
        </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="home-section" style="padding-top:0;">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>Start here</h2>
    <p class="home-section__lede">
      Four workflows added in this round, each one a stage a production siting pipeline needs and most
      screening scripts skip.
    </p>
    <ul class="home-cards" style="list-style:none; padding:0;">
      {% set picks = [
        { "url": "/core-energy-gis-data-spatial-fundamentals/environmental-constraint-and-exclusion-screening/",
          "title": "Environmental Constraint &amp; Exclusion Screening",
          "desc": "Union the constraint layers once, measure in an equal-area frame, and publish an accounting that reconciles.",
          "color": "#345B8B", "icon": "globe" },
        { "url": "/grid-infrastructure-network-proximity-analysis/grid-routing-and-least-cost-path-analysis/",
          "title": "Grid Routing &amp; Least-Cost Path Analysis",
          "desc": "Turn a straight-line interconnection distance into a routable corridor with a cost surface you can defend.",
          "color": "#3D8B5F", "icon": "grid" },
        { "url": "/solar-wind-resource-modeling-workflows/wind-farm-layout-and-wake-modeling/",
          "title": "Wind Farm Layout &amp; Wake Modeling",
          "desc": "Place turbines under real spacing constraints and price the energy the array takes from itself.",
          "color": "#F4A261", "icon": "sun" },
        { "url": "/core-energy-gis-data-spatial-fundamentals/spatial-pipeline-orchestration-and-deployment/",
          "title": "Spatial Pipeline Orchestration &amp; Deployment",
          "desc": "Pinned GDAL and PROJ, idempotent partitions, and the four log fields that catch a spatial regression.",
          "color": "#345B8B", "icon": "globe" }
      ] %}
      {% for p in picks %}
        <li class="home-card" style="--card-c: {{ p.color }};">
          <a class="home-card__head" href="{{ site.url }}{{ p.url }}" style="text-decoration:none; color:inherit;">
            {{ icon(p.icon, p.color) }}
            <h3>{{ p.title | safe }}</h3>
          </a>
          <p>{{ p.desc | safe }}</p>
          <a class="home-card__more" href="{{ site.url }}{{ p.url }}">Read the workflow {{ icon('arrow', 'currentColor') }}</a>
        </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
